## CHANGELOG

### 2025-08-27

Initial version published.


### 2026-08-25

Unreleased changes:

- **Reconnecting sockets.** Each socket owns its lifecycle: it connects
  itself on spawn and retries with full-jitter exponential backoff
  (default 500ms..30s, infinite attempts) after any failure. Sockets are
  `permanent` children, so crashes respawn into an immediate reconnect
  instead of leaving blank zombies.
- **Resubscribe on reconnect.** `RelayAgent` now stores serialized REQ
  payloads (`%{relay => %{sub_id => payload}}`) as the source of truth;
  sockets replay them after every successful handshake. Subscriptions
  recorded while a relay is down are kept (outage-queued) and apply once
  the relay returns; only a genuine relay `CLOSED` removes an entry.
- **Lifecycle notifications.** `NostrEx.listen(:relay_events)` receives
  `{:relay_up, name}`, `{:relay_down, name, reason}` and
  `{:retry_scheduled, name, attempt, delay_ms}`.
- **API changes:**
  - `NostrEx.connect/2` accepts options: `:readiness_timeout`,
    `:backoff_min`, `:backoff_max`, `:max_attempts`.
  - A relay that is down at connect time stays registered and retrying
    instead of returning an error and disappearing; `connect/2` only
    waits for the *first* handshake.
  - `NostrEx.Socket.connect/1-2` removed (connection is internalized).
  - Unified fan-out error contract across `send_event`/`send_sub`/
    `close_sub`: `{:ok, value, failures}` / `{:error, reason, failures}`;
    unknown `send_via` entries appear in failures as
    `{input, :not_connected}` instead of being silently dropped.
  - Dead-relay sends return `{:error, :relay_down}` / `{:error,
    :send_timeout}` rather than crashing the caller.
- **BREAKING: publish acknowledgements are no longer broadcast globally.**
  The old global `:ok` topic is gone (`NostrEx.listen(:ok)` raises).
  Listen on the per-event topic instead - `NostrEx.listen({:ok, event_id})`
  before sending - and receive one
  `{:publish_ack, event_id, %{event_id:, success:, message:, relay:}}`
  message per targeted relay. Relay rejections are additionally logged at
  warning level.
